<title>UK: Stanley Leisure buys UK betting shop group.</title>
<headline>Stanley Leisure buys UK betting shop group.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>British leisure services group Stanley Leisure Plc said on Monday its unit Stanley Racing Ltd agreed to buy British betting shop group James Lane (Bookmakers) Ltd, Pandashield Ltd and its subsidiary Daniel McLaren Ltd.</p>
<p>Stanley Leisure said it would pay 8.0 million pounds initially for the group, which operates 30 betting shops in London. The price comprises an initial cash price of 5.45 million pounds and the assumption of 2.55 million of liabilities, Stanley Leisure said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
